      "seconds_since_start": 10.096,
      "seconds_since_previous_block": 0.081
    },
    "text": "To trace this down I'll need a few specifics \u2014 Lake Formation denials usually trace through several layers (grants, resource links, cross-account shares, IAM, S3, KMS), and pinpointing the right one depends on exactly who's being denied and on what.\n\nCould you share:\n1. **Principal** \u2014 the IAM role/user ARN that's getting denied\n2. **Target resource** \u2014 database and table name (and account/region it lives in)\n3. **Query engine** \u2014 Athena, EMR, Redshift Spectrum, QuickSight, or Glue ETL\n4. **Cross-account?** \u2014 is the querying principal in a different account than the table owner?\n\nOnce I have those, I'll walk the authorization chain (Lake Formation grant scope \u2192 resource links \u2192 cross-account RAM share \u2192 IAM policy simulation \u2192 S3 bucket policy \u2192 KMS key policy) and pinpoint exactly which layer is blocking you."
